    {
      "id": "major-scales-introduction",
      "title": "Major Scales — Introduction",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** theory | **Tier:** intro | **Difficulty:** 1/10 | **Time:** ~20 min\n**Prerequisites:** none\n**Tags:** scales, major, foundations"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "The major scale is the foundational pitch collection of Western music and of much folk and session repertoire. This tier names the pattern, scale degrees, and the leading tone — concepts you will revisit in every later harmony and ear-training lesson."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "the-wwhwwwh-pattern",
      "title": "The WWHWWWH pattern",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A major scale follows **whole–whole–half–whole–whole–whole–half** between consecutive degrees.\n\nFrom **C**: C D E F G A B C — no accidentals.\n\nFrom **G**: one sharp (F♯). From **F**: one flat (B♭). The *pattern* is invariant; only the starting note and key signature change."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scale-degree-names",
      "title": "Scale degree names",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "| Degree | Name | Role |\n|--------|------|------|\n| 1 | tonic | home |\n| 5 | dominant | tension toward tonic |\n| 7 | leading tone | semitone below tonic; pulls upward |\n| 8 | octave | return |\n\nA phrase ending on scale degree 7 feels unresolved — you will hear this again in cadence lessons."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "first-hearing-goal",
      "title": "First hearing goal",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Sing or play one major scale in C, G, and D. Name the intervals as whole or half steps between adjacent notes."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
