  "reading_list": [],
  "quiz_markdown": "### Q1. Major scale interval pattern:\n\n- A) WWHWWWH\n- B) WHWWHWW\n- C) WWWHWWH\n- D) WHWWWHW\n\n**Answer:** A\n\n### Q2. The seventh degree in major is called the leading tone.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q3. G major has one sharp: F♯.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q4. Scale degree 1 is called:\n\n- A) Tonic\n- B) Dominant\n- C) Mediant\n- D) Subdominant\n\n**Answer:** A\n\n### Q5. A major scale from F requires one flat.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q6. The distance from B to C in C major is:\n\n- A) Half step\n- B) Whole step\n- C) Minor third\n- D) Perfect fourth\n\n**Answer:** A\n\n### Q7. Octave is scale degree 8.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q8. Session keys often include G and D major.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q9. WWHWWWH means two whole steps, then a half step, then three whole steps, then a half step.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q10. Leading tone sits a semitone below the tonic.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q11. C major uses only white keys on piano.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q12. Changing the starting note while keeping WWHWWWH changes the key but not the major quality.\n\n**Answer:** True",
